{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:full-critical-covariance",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For the full scores from def:full-score-covariance, including the harmonic translation score and the covariance between the leading and generated-target responses within each control cell, \\(\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal F_s}\\lVert\\Sigma_{h_n}(P)-V(P)\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\\to0\\), where \\(V(P)=\\operatorname{diag}(V_1,\\ldots,V_J)\\), \\(V_j=w_j\\sqrt{\\det H(y_j)}H(y_j)/(4\\pi f_{T1}(y_j))\\), and \\(w_j=\\alpha(y_j)(\\rho_{C0}^{-1}+\\rho_{C1}^{-1})+\\rho_{T0}^{-1}+\\rho_{T1}^{-1}\\). The normalized harmonic variance and every Green--harmonic cross-covariance vanish by the uniform \\(L^2\\) bound in thm:nested-derivative.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal F_s\\)",
      "\\(\\Sigma_h(P)\\)",
      "\\(h_n\\)",
      "\\(V(P)\\)",
      "\\(J\\)",
      "\\(j\\)",
      "\\(H\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal Y_J\\)",
      "\\(f_g\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(\\rho_g\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal H_P\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:four-sample-design",
      "ass:cell-ratios",
      "ass:fixed-separated-grid",
      "ass:outer-ellipticity",
      "ass:lift-regularity",
      "ass:polynomial-bandwidth",
      "lem:bandwidth-feasibility",
      "lem:uniform-critical-estimates",
      "def:nested-derivative",
      "def:full-score-covariance",
      "thm:nested-derivative",
      "ass:density-positivity"
    ],
    "justification": "The proved parametrix and transformed-coordinate calculation deliver the exact four-cell critical blocks while retaining harmonic and generated-target finite-bandwidth terms.",
    "gap": "The result goes beyond the published uniform-law critical calculation by handling variable coefficients, nonlinear pullbacks, and both appearances of each control-cell noise.",
    "consumer": "The closed form is both the inferential variance and a diagnostic benchmark for the adjoint implementation.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\in\\mathcal F_s\\), a grid point \\(y=y_j\\), and write\n\\(x=R_0(y)\\).  The pushforward identities are\n\\[\n f_{C1}(p(x))\\det S(x)=f_{C0}(x),\\qquad\n q(T(y))\\det H(y)=f_{T1}(y),\\qquad\n q(p(x))\\det S(x)=f_{T0}(x).\n \\tag{40}\n\\]\nSince \\(T(y)=p(x)\\), \\(D(y)=S(x)^{-1}H(y)\\), and\n\\(\\alpha(y)=f_{T0}(x)/f_{C0}(x)\\), (40) implies\n\\[\n f_{C0}(x)\\det D(y)=f_{C1}(T(y))\\det H(y)\n =\\frac{f_{T1}(y)}{\\alpha(y)},\n \\qquad f_{T0}(x)\\det D(y)=f_{T1}(y).\n \\tag{41}\n\\]\nEvery division is valid by ass:density-positivity.  In the order-minus-one\npart of def:nested-derivative the two control noises have multiplier\n\\(\\alpha(y)\\), while the treated-pre and treated-post noises have\nmultipliers of absolute value one.  After squaring and applying (41),\ntheir local source intensities in treated-post coordinates are,\nrespectively,\n\\[\n \\alpha(y)f_{T1}(y),\\quad \\alpha(y)f_{T1}(y),\\quad\n f_{T1}(y),\\quad f_{T1}(y).\n \\tag{42}\n\\]\n\nBy lem:uniform-critical-estimates, replacing the exact transformed scores\nby their frozen-pole versions changes each cellwise covariance by\n\\(O(\\sqrt{L_n})+1\\): the exact-versus-frozen error is \\(O(1)\\) in\n\\(L^2\\), while each leading score has norm \\(O(\\sqrt{L_n})\\).  The same\nlemma gives \\(O(1)\\) variance for the order-minus-two term.  The harmonic\nscore has \\(O(1)\\) variance by thm:nested-derivative; its covariance with\na leading score is \\(O(\\sqrt{L_n})\\) by Cauchy--Schwarz.  Hence all these\nterms vanish after division by \\(L_n\\), although none is deleted from the\nfinite-bandwidth score.\n\nFor \\(B_0=B(y)\\), equation (27) in\nlem:uniform-critical-estimates gives the local matrix\n\\[\n \\frac{B(y)^{-1}}{4\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B(y)}}L_n+O(1).\n \\tag{43}\n\\]\nIndependence in ass:four-sample-design makes the four cell covariances\nadd, and ass:cell-ratios supplies their weights.  Combining (42)--(43)\ntherefore gives the \\(j\\)-th diagonal block\n\\[\n \\left\\{\\alpha(y)(\\rho_{C0}^{-1}+\\rho_{C1}^{-1})\n +\\rho_{T0}^{-1}+\\rho_{T1}^{-1}\\right\\}\n f_{T1}(y)\\frac{B(y)^{-1}}{4\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B(y)}}.\n \\tag{44}\n\\]\nSince \\(B(y)=f_{T1}(y)H(y)^{-1}\\), (44) equals\n\\[\n V_j=\\frac{\\left\\{\\alpha(y)(\\rho_{C0}^{-1}+\\rho_{C1}^{-1})\n +\\rho_{T0}^{-1}+\\rho_{T1}^{-1}\\right\\}\n \\sqrt{\\det H(y)}H(y)}{4\\pi f_{T1}(y)}.\n \\tag{45}\n\\]\nFor \\(j\\ne k\\), lem:uniform-critical-estimates and\nass:fixed-separated-grid give only an \\(O(1)\\) product integral because\nthe two poles remain uniformly separated in every observation cell.\nThus every off-diagonal block divided by \\(L_n\\) tends to zero.  The\nconstants are uniform over \\(\\mathcal F_s\\), so assembling the finitely\nmany blocks proves\n\\[\n \\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal F_s}\n \\lVert\\Sigma_{h_n}(P)-V(P)\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nThis calculation includes the covariance between the direct and\ngenerated-target appearances of each control noise; independent-cell\nsampling removes only cross-cell covariance and cannot cancel (45).",
